toni: FYI hitting a parity/format snag in the sampleapp rerank onboarding. Node SDK returns binary/base64 embeddings when calls are batched, python returns numeric arrays. rerank expects number[] and crashes.

toni: node error: TypeError: candidate.embedding is undefined
toni: stack:
```
TypeError: candidate.embedding is undefined
    at scoreCandidates (/workspace/sampleapp/lib/rerank.js:42:20)
    at processTicksAndRejections (internal/process/task_queues.js:95:5)
```

ash: can you paste the raw payloads from both SDKs for the same 2-item input?
toni: python (working):
```
[{"id":"d-1","embedding":[0.00012,-0.213,0.0034,...],"model":"open-embed-1536"},{"id":"d-2","embedding":[0.00011,0.198,0.002,...],"model":"open-embed-1536"}]
```

toni: node (weird):
```
[{"id":"d-1","vec_bytes":"QkFTRTY0X0JBVFNfRVhBTVBM...","model":"open-embed-1536"},{"id":"d-2","vec_bytes":"QkFTRTY0X0JBVFNfRVhBTVBM...","model":"open-embed-1536"}]
```

sam: aha. that's a different flavor of mismatch — node is returning per-item base64-encoded raw float32 bytes in `vec_bytes` for batched responses (optimisation to reduce JSON size), while python returns `embedding: number[]`. single-item node calls still return `embedding` numeric arrays as before, so this only shows up for arrays (>1).

toni: exactly. whole onboarding flow fails because our rerank expects the numeric array shape.

ash: any idea why? recent batching helper change to compress payloads? or the transport layer switched to sending binary per item?
sam: likely the batching helper switched to serializing each vector as raw Float32 binary then base64 to keep per-item size down. That itself is fine but we forgot to document/rehydrate it in the client-to-app surface. There's also a retry middleware that might double-encode in rare retry cases, so you can end up with a double-base64 string which complicates quick decoding.

toni: repro (node):
```js
// repro
const res = await client.embeddings.create({ model: 'open-embed-1536', input: ['one','two'] })
console.log(res)
// observed: res[0].vec_bytes -> "QkFTRTY0..."
```

ash: short-term workaround for onboarding/sampleapp: decode base64 -> Float32Array -> convert to plain number[] and map to embedding before feeding rerank. e.g.:
```js
function decodeVecBase64(b64) {
  const buf = Buffer.from(b64, 'base64');
  // use the underlying ArrayBuffer to create a Float32Array view
  const floats = new Float32Array(buf.buffer, buf.byteOffset, Math.floor(buf.byteLength / 4));
  // convert typed array to plain number[] so downstream code doesn't mutate the underlying buffer
  return Array.from(floats);
}
// normalize response
const normalized = res.map(item => {
  if (item.vec_bytes) {
    return { ...item, embedding: decodeVecBase64(item.vec_bytes) };
  }
  return item; // already embedding:number[] from single-input or python
});
```

toni: confirmed this workaround unblocks the sampleapp e2e and the rerank path. pushed a tiny snippet to the sampleapp quickstart and filed PR redwood/devex#2044 with the note for onboarding pages.

ci-bot: CI: sampleapp-embed-shape-integration failed — expected embedding:number[] but saw vec_bytes:string in node samples.

sam: plan: 1) patch Node SDK batching helper to expose an option to return numeric arrays by default (or keep `vec_bytes` but include `embedding` fallback decoded on client) 2) add an integration parity test that runs python vs node sample flows and fails the build if shapes differ 3) audit retry middleware to prevent double-encoding on retries.

ash: can we make the SDK decode automatically by default? that reduces onboarding friction.
sam: yes, will land a safe default: the node SDK will decode vec_bytes into embedding:number[] before returning to apps and log a short deprecation note if vec_bytes is present. We'll add a performance knob for teams that want raw bytes.

toni: thanks — please add a short note in the onboarding troubleshooting doc so support can point folks to the fix/workaround until the patch ships.

sam: assigning myself for the SDK patch + tests. target: patch release tonight after unit tests. adding an e2e CI job that sanity-checks node vs python sampleapp output shapes.

toni: thanks all. saved the workaround snippet into onboarding and linked PR 2044. tagging @sam for follow-up on retry double-encoding. :rocket:
